## Report
Disposition update:
- The original reasoning about `InputUnavailable` was accurate.
- The conclusion that this is a local authorization bypass was not.
- AWS exhibits the same behavior when ABAC is disabled, so Argmin is aligned.

Summary of evidence:
- Policy requests for objects always set bucket tags to Unavailable (crates/auth/src/bucket_policy.rs:287-303), and bucket tag loading is gated on bucket_abac_enabled in server-core (crates/server-core/src/coordinator/authz.rs:846-878).
- s3:BucketTag/* is registered as a supported condition key (crates/auth/src/bucket_policy/condition_key.rs:102-108). When tags are unavailable, resolve_bucket_tag returns ResolvedValue::Unavailable (crates/auth/src/bucket_policy/condition_key.rs:217-222), which becomes ConditionMatchResult::InputUnavailable (crates/auth/src/bucket_policy/condition_key.rs:423-427). InputUnavailable causes the statement to have no effect, even for Deny (crates/auth/src/bucket_policy.rs:602-606).
Dynamic PoC:
- Local evaluator regression now lives in `crates/auth/src/bucket_policy.rs:get_object_bucket_tag_deny_condition_is_nonoperative_when_bucket_tags_unavailable` and confirms that a `Deny` conditioned on `s3:BucketTag/security` is skipped when bucket tags are unavailable, leaving the unconditional `Allow` effective.
- AWS-backed regression now lives in `crates/s3-tests/tests/bucket_policy.rs:test_bucket_policy_get_object_bucket_tag_deny_condition_when_abac_disabled` and confirms the same behavior against Amazon S3.
Attempts per rubric:
- Crash attempt: built/runs succeeded; no crash expected for logic bug.
- Valgrind: not installed (`valgrind: command not found`).
- Debugger: lldb ran the test binary successfully (no crash, but confirms execution under debugger).

